{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Well, after about 3 or 4 episodes of Kotter, you and your friends decide to check out what else is going on in the house. You head downstairs to the rec room, (isnt that what we called them in the 70s?) Folks are cutting rugs into the Shag carpeting, doing a dance step that was all the rage in the Mid 70s! What dance is everyone most likely doing?","The Hustle"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"music\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Your cellphone starts ringing (well, actually playing your favorite 70s tune). Its one of your friends next door at the 80s house. They want you to come over right away! When you get there, theyre in a quandary. See, they have to name that tune from one-hit-wonder artist, Staci Q. It was popular around 1986. Which one was it?","Two of Hearts"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"music\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["An argument ensues amidst the Fondue, about when the Old School rap group Sugar Hill Gang released their hit Rappers Delight. You seem to vaguely recall that it was released sometime in the 70s, but your friend is insistent on the fact that it was released in the early 80s! After some debate, you both agree that it was probably released in the early 80s,since thats when it was receiving a lot of airplay. Is this True or False?","False"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"music\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["You see the crowds really thinning at Place du la 70s, so you thank your hosts and head on back over to the House of 80s for one last look! When you trek back in, you see things are winding down here as well. But wait, someones stuck yet another tape in the VCR (it IS an 80s party, after all! Only, not Beta!) Holy smokes! Its a 90s tape of P.T. Andersons 70s Era film Boogie Nights! You and your friends are too tired to stay and watch this masterpiece, but on the drive home, you seem to recall that it did have a couple of 80s groups and their songs on it! What were two of the more memorable Artists/ Tunes in this film?","Sister Christian by Nightranger and Jesses Girl by Rick Springfield"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"music\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
